 "intro": "Asculum in Picenum, 89 BC. The Social War began here when the townspeople killed every Roman in the town. You are the consul Gnaeus Pompeius Strabo, besieging it. Your seventeen-year-old son, the future Pompey the Great, serves with you.",
 "debrief": "Appian and other writers report that Strabo defeated a large Italian relief army before Asculum. The Italian commander Judacilius, a native of the town, broke through to it with a few cohorts, but finding it starving and hopeless, killed his enemies, built a pyre in a temple and poisoned himself. Asculum surrendered; its leaders were executed and its people expelled. The young Pompey’s name appears on an inscription listing Strabo’s staff. The other choices are what-ifs.",
